claim: The asynchronous connect path no longer performs any cleanup of the session on failure or on destruction, and the queued lambda captures the session but never destroys it if the bridge is destroyed beforehand, leaving a dangling frame callback and leaking the session.; file: app/qttunebridge.cpp; quote:     QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [this, uri, err, session]() {
        // JOIN FIRST, then clear the flag, then emit: assigning to a
        // joinable std::thread terminates the process, and a QML
        // handler can run SYNCHRONOUSLY inside connectingChanged —
        if (m_connectThread.joinable()) {
            m_connectThread.join();
        }
        m_connecting = false;
        emit connectingChanged();
    });

